Hey Missy,

Sorry we missed your call last night.  I was not home and Todd was up to his eyeballs in cleaning up a plumbing problem that we had and still have at our house.  Boy, was I glad I was gone last night.

Alice had invited me to go to a gala that her book club put on last night at the Omni Hotel.  It was nice, but long.  They featured the poetry and readings of Thomas Melancon.  Have you hear of him, he was there, very good, although I am not a "poetry kinda sistah", but it doesn't cost much to be considerate and supportive of other folks' passion.  Anyway, it was sooooo much fun getting all dressed up, the attire was semi-formal.  When I got dressed and came out of the bedroom, Jordan goes "Oooohhhhh Mommy, Todd says nothing......needless to say Jordan made my evening.  He is really going to be the kind of guy that looks out for his Mom.

As far as Todd goes, I'm trying so hard, I remember you saying "be still" and I have been, but boy it gets hard sometimes.  Alot of times, I feel so confident about breaking out of my own, after all, it could not be much different.  Sometimes my mind says do it now, since the stock markets are down and I am broke at this time (laugh).  Anyway, I'm semi-cool.

What's up with you?  Any more phone calls from Mr. Yoga?  I heard it's supposed to be cool, weatherwise, for you guys over the next couple of days.  When I went over to your Dad's house, Nell said that you had your hard "pressed" for the wedding.  Are you still wearing it "pressed"?  You go girl!

See ya!
